Manage the purge webhooks of a distribution

Usage:
  nexoctl cache webhook [flags]
  nexoctl cache webhook [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a purge webhook to a distribution
  list        List the purge webhooks of a distribution
  remove      Remove a purge webhook
  test        Call a purge webhook once (connection test)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for webhook

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl cache webhook [command] --help" for more information about a command.
